      "name": "Manggus",
      "aliases": [
        "Mangus",
        "Manggus-Râkshasa"
      ],
      "domain": [
        "Ogres",
        "Shape-shifting",
        "Devouring"
      ],
      "description": "\"Mongolian name for Râkschasas\" (Busk's note): ogres who take false shapes to get close to their prey. In the Mongol sagas a male and a female Manggus come as a he-goat and a beautiful maiden; taken in by seven royal brothers, they devour one brother's life each year until only the Khan is left, and the Pig's-head soothsayer is sent for to save him.",
      "spectralCoordinates": {
